# Secrets: exactly the one secret-path list,
# secrets.GitignorePatterns() in internal/extensions/tools/api/secrets, from
# this comment to the next blank line - the secret-scan test refuses a missing
# entry, an extra one, and a secret pattern ignored elsewhere in this file
# (add it to the list instead, so the hook refuses it too). Secrets by purpose (.env.build,
# .env.test): Claude copies them, never reads them. The pre-commit hook
# (.githooks/pre-commit, make hooks) refuses a secret staged anyway.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.secret/
.secrets/
**/hub/keys/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.token
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
.netrc
.pgpass
.git-credentials

# Cloud sync folders (hygiene, not secrets)
.dropbox/
.dropbox.cache/
.stfolder/
.stversions/

# Build artifacts
/ktw-*.exe
katyoti-preview/
/terminal/
/marketplace/

# Demo world — scripts/demo/, rebuilt by demo-reset.sh
.demo/

# A CWM workspace bootstrapped at the REPOSITORY ROOT is always a mistake.
# The real workspace is `.katyoti/cwm/`; these appear when something points the
# service at the repo itself, which used to happen on every
# `go test ./internal/extensions/cwm/...`. Ignored so a stray bootstrap can
# never be committed again, even if a future caller reintroduces one.
/config/
/cwm/
